    "documents": [
      {
        "body": "SYNTHETIC DEMONSTRATION ONLY. Original fictional water-quality sample\nlogistics station, not a water treatment or public-health decision system.\nEvery need, obligation, threshold, component, allocation and operation is a\nfictional demonstration choice, not real accepted engineering intent.\nBoundary: container intake records, identification holds and custody handoff.\nExcludes collection chemistry, analytical validity, refrigeration, contamination,\nequipment reliability, physical security, clinical and public-health suitability.\nCandidate A: staffed local register; candidate B: offline station with local\nreceipts and later synchronization. B is the demonstrated concept, not a\nreal engineering selection. Offline synchronization remains qualitative.\nOpen questions: real custody policy, label reconciliation authority, storage\nduration, power budget and environmental limits require stakeholder work. ",
        "line": 5,
        "owner": "WaterSampling",
        "owner_kind": "Package",
        "source": "examples/engineering-gallery/water-sampling/station.sysml"
      },
      {
        "body": "CSE-CLOCK/2.0\nperiod 1 second ",
        "line": 17,
        "name": "cseClock",
        "owner": "WaterSampling",
        "owner_kind": "Package",
        "source": "examples/engineering-gallery/water-sampling/station.sysml"
      },
      {
        "body": "Fictional candidate components: panel accepts requests; register\npreserves provisional or reconciled receipts; rack holds containers.\nThese declarations establish composition only, not connector topology,\nimplementation or physical capacity. A provisional receipt may state\nHELD with identity unresolved; it never authorizes pickup. ",
        "line": 23,
        "owner": "WaterSampling::Station",
        "owner_kind": "PartDefinition",
        "source": "examples/engineering-gallery/water-sampling/station.sysml"
      },
      {
        "body": "CSE-INT/2.0\nrange 0 20 scale 1 unit second ",
        "line": 34,
        "name": "cseType",
        "owner": "WaterSampling::Station::processingElapsed",
        "owner_kind": "AttributeUsage",
        "source": "examples/engineering-gallery/water-sampling/station.sysml"
      },
      {
        "body": "Fictional stakeholder need: The operator needs sample identity preserved through custody transfer. ",
        "line": 47,
        "owner": "WaterSampling::PreserveIdentity",
        "owner_kind": "ConcernUsage",
        "requirement": "WaterSampling::PreserveIdentity",
        "source": "examples/engineering-gallery/water-sampling/station.sysml"
      },
      {
        "body": "Fictional stakeholder need: The courier needs a reconciled record of containers accepted for pickup. ",
        "line": 48,
        "owner": "WaterSampling::AccountForContainers",
        "owner_kind": "ConcernUsage",
        "requirement": "WaterSampling::AccountForContainers",
        "source": "examples/engineering-gallery/water-sampling/station.sysml"
      },
      {
        "body": "Fictional stakeholder need: The custodian needs a declared intake pause and controlled restoration. ",
        "line": 49,
        "owner": "WaterSampling::RecoverService",
        "owner_kind": "ConcernUsage",
        "requirement": "WaterSampling::RecoverService",
        "source": "examples/engineering-gallery/water-sampling/station.sysml"
      },
      {
        "body": "Nominal: present labeled container; record receipt; match pickup manifest; record custody transfer. Success means a documentary transfer record, not analytical sample validity. These are documentary exchanges, not executable SysML guards/effects. ",
        "line": 63,
        "owner": "WaterSampling::TransferLabeledSample",
        "owner_kind": "UseCaseUsage",
        "source": "examples/engineering-gallery/water-sampling/station.sysml"
      },
      {
        "body": "Exception and recovery: unreadable label leads to hold; operator supplies corrected identity; station records reconciliation before release. Reconciliation authority is fictional and requires real policy work. These are documentary exchanges, not executable SysML guards/effects. ",
        "line": 64,
        "owner": "WaterSampling::RecoverUnidentifiedSample",
        "owner_kind": "UseCaseUsage",
        "source": "examples/engineering-gallery/water-sampling/station.sysml"
      },
      {
        "body": "Lifecycle: declare pause; suspend intake; inspect and restore equipment; record return to service. No physical repair simulation or reliability claim. These are documentary exchanges, not executable SysML guards/effects. ",
        "line": 65,
        "owner": "WaterSampling::RestoreStation",
        "owner_kind": "UseCaseUsage",
        "source": "examples/engineering-gallery/water-sampling/station.sysml"
      },
      {
